 outside 62-76%. It also credits Marco Silva with 19.2% of exposure and presents him as the best active reviewer. That violates the criterion that no active person is a real code expert there.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives Kochnev 77.0% of delegators, which is in range, and says nobody active owns any of it. But for delegator.rb it credits Marco Silva with 16.7%, and it frames the delegator code as including delegator.rb. For the delegators/ directory itself it follows the original authors, but it names Silva as the active contact.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 117 lines, 100% of grouped_exposure.rb, rather than crediting Kochnev. That fails the copied-file attribution.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A says 89.3% of lines belong to departed people, which is outside the 79-90% range only at the edge, so that part is fine. It excludes the copyright commit and dependabot gets 5 lines, so a bot is credited with lines. It also does not state Peter Scholz's departed share or Subbota's active share in the required way.\",\"pass\":false}], \"B\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B says the top committer differs from the top owner, but it gives no commit or line percentages, and it says Doubrovkine doesn't appear among top blame owners. It gives no 31.8% or 5.6% figures.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B recommends Marco Silva as the best reviewer of exposure and does not say Kochnev wrote 62-76%. This presents an active person as the expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B routes delegator review to Lena Brandt and Marco Silva, and gives no percentage for Kochnev. It names active people as the owners.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 143 lines of exposure and does not attribute the copied file to Kochnev. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Lena Brandt with 20 lines and names her as a reviewer, which fails. It gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}], \"C\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C says dblock leads with about 52 commits, and gives no percentages. It also lists dblock as inactive since 2016, which is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Marco Silva as the best-informed active reviewer with 143 blamed lines. That presents an active person as the expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C routes delegator review to Marco Silva. It does note that neither Marco nor Lena wrote the logic, but gives no Kochnev percentage.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C does note that GroupedExposure is a copy of NestingExposure, but it still credits Silva with about 143 lines and does not attribute them to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C treats Lena Brandt as a secondary reviewer, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}], \"D\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D uses churn and a decay score, not surviving lines. It says dblock has the most commits but gives no shares and no Kochnev line ownership.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D routes exposure review to Lena Brandt, who is a mechanical-line contributor, and does not state Kochnev's share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D sends delegator review to Marco and Lena, and gives no Kochnev share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives no line attribution for Marco Silva or grouped_exposure.rb.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D names Lena Brandt as the top reviewer, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}], \"E\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E has dblock at 38 commits and 8.5% of lines, with Kochnev at about 17%. Names were not merged and the numbers fall outside the required ranges.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Kochnev holds 53% of exposure and recommends Marco Silva as the best choice. That is outside 62-76% and presents an active person as the expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 67% of delegators, below the 68-82% range, and names Lena Brandt as owning about 11% of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (143 lines), not Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Lena Brandt with about 11% of delegator lines, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}], \"F\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F says dblock has the most commits and Kochnev the most lines, but gives no shares. It says dblock owns about 38 lines, and its numbers cover only lib/.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F recommends Marco Silva as the best first reviewer of exposure. It lists Kochnev as owning 392 lines without a share. It presents an active person as the expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F makes Lena Brandt the best delegator reviewer with 12 lines, which names an active person as an owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco Silva with 143 exposure lines and does not attribute the copied file to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F treats Lena Brandt as a reviewer with 18 lines, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":14686,"type":"result","duration_ms":14733,"uuid":"2f237f7f-95f6-4f84-9b88-847bd0a9f883","ttft_stream_ms":2020,"time_to_request_ms":516,"first_content_frame_ms":2020,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
